@meta
id: 04-15
title: Drill — down, edit, back up, edit
chapter: 04
type: drill
skills: count-prefix, relativenumber
par: 30
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: two clicks and a scroll
open: staging.env
vimrc: set relativenumber

@brief
Eight times, in this order: append `  # ok` — two spaces, hash, space,
`ok` — to the last line of the file, then append the same thing to the
`WEBHOOK_SECRET` line, then save and quit.

Down with a count, up with a count. No arrow keys, no scrolling. Read the margin both times, because
after the first edit every number on it has changed.

@keys
| `18j` | down eighteen lines |
| `9k` | up nine lines |
| `A` | append at the end of the line |

@hints
The second jump is upward, and its count is not the one you just used.
--
Read, jump, edit, read again. Never reuse a number after you have moved.

@solution
    18j A <space><space># ok <Esc> 9k A <space><space># ok <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Twenty-five keystrokes.

The mistake this drill exists to burn out is reusing a stale number. You
read `18` off the margin, you jump, and the whole margin silently
renumbers itself around your new position. Half of all missed jumps in
your first month will be a number you read before the last move rather
than after it.

@start staging.env
# staging environment
APP_NAME=payments
LOG_LEVEL=debug
PORT=4000
DATABASE_URL=postgres://payments@database:5432/payments
REDIS_URL=redis://cache:6379
QUEUE_PREFIX=staging
PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://sandbox.provider.test
PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
WEBHOOK_SECRET=set-me
RETRY_ATTEMPTS=6
RETRY_BACKOFF_MS=2000
REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS=90
EXPORT_SCHEDULE=0 * * * *
FEATURE_PARTIAL_REFUNDS=false
FEATURE_INSTANT_PAYOUT=false
METRICS_PORT=9100
SENTRY_DSN=
TRACE_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1

@expected staging.env
# staging environment
APP_NAME=payments
LOG_LEVEL=debug
PORT=4000
DATABASE_URL=postgres://payments@database:5432/payments
REDIS_URL=redis://cache:6379
QUEUE_PREFIX=staging
PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://sandbox.provider.test
PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
WEBHOOK_SECRET=set-me  # ok
RETRY_ATTEMPTS=6
RETRY_BACKOFF_MS=2000
REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS=90
EXPORT_SCHEDULE=0 * * * *
FEATURE_PARTIAL_REFUNDS=false
FEATURE_INSTANT_PAYOUT=false
METRICS_PORT=9100
SENTRY_DSN=
TRACE_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1  # ok
